<h1>Nebula Science Fiction</h1>

From <I>Tuck's Encyclopedia of Science Fiction and Fantasy</I>:
<p>
<pre>
      This normally featured one short novel per issue with short stories
    and departments of interest, including film reviews by F. J. Ackerman,
    "Fanorama" by W. Willis, and book reviews by K. Slater. The covers were
    painted by various British artists and always had plenty of colour.
      The magazine was generally quite entertaining, though few stories will
    become classics. Authors included most of the contemporary British writers,
    such as E. C. Tubb, K. Bulmer, E. F. Russell, and W. F. Temple. R.
    Silverberg made his first appearance in any magazine in <i>Nebula</i>.
    R. A. Heinlein was reprinted a number of times.
</pre>

